Coding Questions
1.Given an integer N, generate the character corresponding to each number using the pattern:
1 → C, 2 → F, 3 → I, ...
Every next number moves in the alphabet. After Z, start again from A.
For N = 1 to 20, output the corresponding characters.  


#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
int n;
cin>>n;
for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)
{
char c='A'+((3*i-1)%26);
cout<<c<<" ";
}

}
